// Expressions and types are bounded in how deeply they may nest. Past the bound the parser stops
// recursing, reports it once, and takes the rest of the construct with it, so nothing downstream
// ever walks a tree deeper than the bound and a pathological program is rejected rather than
// exhausting the stack.
// @expect-error This expression nests too deeply to be parsed; split it into smaller expressions
// @expect-error This type nests too deeply to be parsed; reduce how deeply its parentheses and type arguments nest
// @expect-error build failed with 3 problems

